@startuml

title TTA Notifications v0.6 — In-band subscription (receiver-initiated), event notification, follow-up pull\nPOC implementation: component/subscription (docs/tta-notifications-v06/)

box "Receiving organisation — Zonnebloem (Subscription Client)" #E8F4FD
    participant xis_r as "XIS / EHR\n(vendor)"
    participant kp_r as "Knooppunt\n[subscription client]"
end box

box "Addressing"
    participant mcsd as "mCSD Query Directory"
end box

box "Sending organisation — Plataan (Subscription Server)" #FDF2E8
    participant kp_s as "Knooppunt\n[subscription server]"
    participant pdp as "Knooppunt PDP\n+ PIP (local consent records)"
    participant fhir_s as "FHIR store\n(HAPI tenant)"
    participant xis_s as "XIS / EHR\n(vendor)"
end box

== Step 0: agreements (design time, out of band) ==
note over xis_r, xis_s
Pre-agreed between the parties, configured on both knooppunten:
- SubscriptionTopic canonical (http://fhir.nl/SubscriptionTopic/nl-task-notified-pull)
- allowed payload modes (empty, id-only)
- heartbeat terms
Discoverable read-only at GET /fhir/SubscriptionTopic/{id}
end note

== Step 1: authorization basis (sender side) — the vendor supplies it, the knooppunt enforces it ==
alt POC as built: dedicated vendor endpoint
    xis_s -> kp_s : POST /subscription/authorizations\n{receiverUra, topic, patientBsn?, validUntil?}
    note right of kp_s : the "who may be notified of what" record;\nlooked up by the authz hook before activation\nand before every send (POC: stub, logs, always allows)
else alternative: reuse GF Authorization (PDP / PIP)
    xis_s -> pdp : record local consent record on the resource\n(for COW: the Coordination Task naming Task.owner\ncan itself be the record)
    note right of pdp : one basis governs both the notification\nand the follow-up pull; no separate registration.\nThe authz hook then asks the PDP instead of\nits own table — the hook placement stays the same
end

== Step 2: subscription intent (receiver side, in-band creation) ==
xis_r -> kp_r : POST /subscription/intents\n{partnerUra, topic, payloadMode=id-only, heartbeatPeriodSeconds}
activate kp_r
opt no per-partner configuration for {partnerUra}
    kp_r -> mcsd : Organization?identifier=ura|{partnerUra}\n-> Endpoint (payloadType = tta-subscription)
    mcsd --> kp_r : partner FHIR base
end
note right of kp_r : resolution order in the POC:\nper-partner config first, mCSD only as fallback\n(compose and e2e use config)
kp_r -> kp_r : build backport Subscription\n(criteria/_criteria topic-canonical + filter Task.owner=ura|own,\nchannel rest-hook + endpoint + _payload id-only,\nheartbeat-period ext)
kp_r -> kp_s : POST {partnerBase}/Subscription\n[application/fhir+json]
activate kp_s
kp_s -> kp_s : validate: topic in agreed list, mode in allowed modes,\nrest-hook, fhir+json (400 / 422 OperationOutcome)
kp_s -> kp_s : store status=requested
kp_s --> kp_r : 201 Created (Subscription, status=requested)
kp_r -> kp_r : record client subscription (status=requested)
kp_r --> xis_r : 201 {reference, status=requested}
deactivate kp_r

== Step 3: handshake ==
kp_s -> kp_s : authz hook (checkpoint: activation)
kp_s -> kp_r : POST {channel.endpoint}\nBundle(history) / Parameters type=handshake-notification
kp_r --> kp_s : 200 OK
kp_s -> kp_s : status=active
deactivate kp_s
note over kp_s, kp_r : on 4xx/5xx: exponential backoff retry;\npersistent failure -> status=error

== Step 4: event at the sender ==
alt event feed via poller
    xis_s -> fhir_s : POST /Task (COW Coordination Task,\ncode fulfill + use-case code, owner=ura|{receiver})
    kp_s -> fhir_s : GET Task/_history?_since=...  (every pollintervalseconds)
    fhir_s --> kp_s : history Bundle
else event feed via ingest API
    xis_s -> kp_s : POST /subscription/events\n{resourceType=Task, resourceId, interaction, ownerUra}
end
activate kp_s
kp_s -> kp_s : match topic + filter (Task, create/update, owner URA)
kp_s -> kp_s : authz hook + consent hook\n(checkpoint: notification-send)
note right of kp_s : alternative: the hook evaluates\n"may {receiver} be notified of {topic} for {patient}?"\nvia the PDP against the PIP record (see step 1);\nconsent via the Mitz component. Withdrawal = record removed
kp_s -> kp_s : allocate event-number (monotonic, per subscription)\nalias focus: Task/4711 -> Task/<HMAC alias>\nappend to event log
kp_s -> kp_r : POST {channel.endpoint}\nBundle(history) / Parameters type=event-notification\nnotification-event { event-number, timestamp, focus=Task/<alias> }
activate kp_r
kp_r -> kp_r : continuity check (event-number == highest+1)\nidempotency (subscription, event-number)
kp_r -> kp_r : normalise -> inbox entry\n{type=event, eventNumber, focus, topic}
kp_r --> kp_s : 200 OK
deactivate kp_r
deactivate kp_s

== Step 5: follow-up pull (receiver side) ==
xis_r -> kp_r : GET /subscription/inbox
kp_r --> xis_r : [{id, type=event, subscriptionReference, eventNumber, focus=Task/<alias>}]
xis_r -> kp_s : GET {senderBase}/fhir/Task/<alias>
activate kp_s
kp_s -> kp_s : de-alias -> Task/4711
kp_s -> fhir_s : GET Task/4711
fhir_s --> kp_s : Task
kp_s --> xis_r : Task (id rewritten to alias)
deactivate kp_s
note over xis_r, kp_s : the knooppunt is now in the pull/data path —\nthe price of aliasing non-compliant ids (RQ 8)
xis_r -> kp_r : POST /subscription/inbox/{id}/ack

@enduml
